WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.525 --> 00:00:01.526
- Good morning Believe Nation.

00:00:01.526 --> 00:00:02.837
My name is Evan Carmichael.

00:00:02.837 --> 00:00:04.079
My one word is "believe"

00:00:04.079 --> 00:00:05.981
and I believe that
entrepreneurs will solve

00:00:05.981 --> 00:00:07.932
all of the major problems in the world.

00:00:07.932 --> 00:00:12.467
So today's message is be
conscious of your mortality.

00:00:12.467 --> 00:00:14.056
Over to you, Sadhguru.

00:00:14.056 --> 00:00:16.436
(rooster singing)

00:00:16.436 --> 00:00:18.987
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:18.987 --> 00:00:21.627
♫ Espresso keep me going

00:00:21.627 --> 00:00:25.681
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:25.681 --> 00:00:28.066
- You should just observe,

00:00:28.066 --> 00:00:30.649
if every makes a little effort,

00:00:31.504 --> 00:00:36.013
everybody take a little time
for this piece of life, okay?

00:00:36.013 --> 00:00:38.584
Not for your family, not for your kid,

00:00:38.584 --> 00:00:40.592
not for something else, something else,

00:00:40.592 --> 00:00:42.598
just for this piece of life,

00:00:42.598 --> 00:00:44.568
give it little time because this is

00:00:44.568 --> 00:00:48.248
the most important piece of
life in your life, isn't it?

00:00:48.248 --> 00:00:49.192
Yes or no?

00:00:49.192 --> 00:00:50.025
- [Audience] Yes.

00:00:50.025 --> 00:00:51.741
- Even if you're in love with somebody,

00:00:51.741 --> 00:00:56.222
still this is the most important
piece of life, isn't it?

00:00:56.222 --> 00:00:57.637
So pay some attention to it.

00:00:57.637 --> 00:01:01.673
How does it happen? Why have
you taken it for granted?

00:01:01.673 --> 00:01:04.204
Believe me, you're not
going to be here forever.

00:01:04.204 --> 00:01:05.520
I'll bless you with a long life,

00:01:05.520 --> 00:01:08.408
but you're going to fall dead one day.

00:01:08.408 --> 00:01:09.741
Yes or no?
- Yes.

00:01:11.103 --> 00:01:13.824
- So, do not take this for granted.

00:01:13.824 --> 00:01:14.989
If you wake up in the morning,

00:01:14.989 --> 00:01:17.982
tomorrow IF you wake up in the morning ...

00:01:17.982 --> 00:01:20.807
(audience laughing)

00:01:20.807 --> 00:01:23.834
It's not my wish, but I want you to know,

00:01:23.834 --> 00:01:26.718
of all the people who go to bed tonight

00:01:26.718 --> 00:01:30.885
over a million people will
not wake up tomorrow morning.

00:01:31.770 --> 00:01:35.856
And tomorrow, if you and me
wake up tomorrow morning,

00:01:35.856 --> 00:01:38.230
is it not a fantastic thing?

00:01:38.230 --> 00:01:41.261
A million people did not
wake up, you woke up.

00:01:41.261 --> 00:01:42.789
Is it not a great thing?

00:01:42.789 --> 00:01:43.676
- [Audience] Yes.

00:01:43.676 --> 00:01:47.838
- Just look at the ceiling and
smile, you are still awake.

00:01:47.838 --> 00:01:50.962
You're still there.
(audience applauding)

00:01:50.962 --> 00:01:54.695
And for many, many millions of people

00:01:54.695 --> 00:01:57.898
somebody who's dear to
them did not wake up,

00:01:57.898 --> 00:02:01.299
so just check those five,
six people around you.

00:02:01.299 --> 00:02:05.589
Did all woke up? Wow,
it's a fantastic day!

00:02:05.589 --> 00:02:08.327
You woke up, and everybody
who matters to you

00:02:08.327 --> 00:02:10.335
around you woke up.

00:02:10.335 --> 00:02:13.137
Is it not a fantastic day?

00:02:13.137 --> 00:02:14.583
You don't think so.

00:02:14.583 --> 00:02:16.523
- Yes. Yes.
(audience laughing)

00:02:16.523 --> 00:02:18.776
- You don't seem to think so.

00:02:18.776 --> 00:02:21.532
Because the problem is just this,

00:02:21.532 --> 00:02:26.078
you are living with an
idea that you're immortal.

00:02:26.078 --> 00:02:27.399
When I say you're immortal

00:02:27.399 --> 00:02:29.938
you're not actually
thinking you're immortal,

00:02:29.938 --> 00:02:33.380
but you're not conscious
of your mortality.

00:02:33.380 --> 00:02:35.602
If you're not conscious of your mortality

00:02:35.602 --> 00:02:38.531
somebody will think
you're immortal, isn't it?

00:02:38.531 --> 00:02:40.055
How many moments in a day

00:02:40.055 --> 00:02:43.245
are you conscious that you're mortal?

00:02:43.245 --> 00:02:47.012
If you were conscious,
would you have time to grip?

00:02:47.012 --> 00:02:49.755
Would have to time to fight with somebody?

00:02:49.755 --> 00:02:53.328
Would you have time to do
something lavish with your life?

00:02:53.328 --> 00:02:56.711
If you knew, if you were
conscious that you're mortal

00:02:56.711 --> 00:03:00.572
you would do nothing other
than what's absolutely needed

00:03:00.572 --> 00:03:03.045
for you and everybody around you.

00:03:03.045 --> 00:03:04.668
This one thing, if you do,

00:03:04.668 --> 00:03:06.742
if you just remind yourself --

00:03:06.742 --> 00:03:08.269
Don't think this is a negative thing,

00:03:08.269 --> 00:03:09.385
death is not a negative thing,

00:03:09.385 --> 00:03:12.364
it's the only thing which
has added value to your life.

00:03:12.364 --> 00:03:16.002
If you're here forever
you would be unbearable.

00:03:16.002 --> 00:03:18.852
- Yes, yes.
(audience laughing)

00:03:18.852 --> 00:03:23.575
- Isn't it? Why aren't we
glad everybody dies one day?

00:03:23.575 --> 00:03:27.580
If you just become
conscious of this one thing,

00:03:27.580 --> 00:03:30.207
that always you're
conscious that I'm mortal,

00:03:30.207 --> 00:03:31.584
you don't have to think I will die today,

00:03:31.584 --> 00:03:34.458
we don't intend, we want
to live as far as possible,

00:03:34.458 --> 00:03:36.707
just know one day I will die.

00:03:36.707 --> 00:03:38.977
If you're just conscious of this one thing

00:03:38.977 --> 00:03:40.931
you will naturally become spiritual.

00:03:40.931 --> 00:03:43.213
Everyday, every moment,
if you remind yourself,

00:03:43.213 --> 00:03:47.536
"This is a brief life. I'm
mortal, one day it will end".

00:03:47.536 --> 00:03:50.532
Just do this for two days
and see you will become

00:03:50.532 --> 00:03:52.570
something truly fantastic within yourself.

00:03:52.570 --> 00:03:54.472
Just, this is all true.

00:03:54.472 --> 00:03:56.015
- Simply beautiful.

00:03:56.015 --> 00:03:57.642
- That's all that's needed.

00:03:57.642 --> 00:04:00.809
If you want to know the value of life,

00:04:01.955 --> 00:04:04.393
just know that it's a brief happening.

00:04:04.393 --> 00:04:06.181
- I think it's easy to lose perspective

00:04:06.181 --> 00:04:07.796
of how great the life you have.

00:04:07.796 --> 00:04:09.771
Just the fact that you
are watching this video,

00:04:09.771 --> 00:04:11.296
you have access to the Internet,

00:04:11.296 --> 00:04:13.257
you are investing time in yourself,

00:04:13.257 --> 00:04:14.980
in learning, in trying to get better,

00:04:14.980 --> 00:04:17.753
puts you ahead of most
people in the world.

00:04:17.753 --> 00:04:20.920
And the problems that you
have pale in comparison

00:04:20.920 --> 00:04:24.278
to most of the other people in the world.

00:04:24.278 --> 00:04:26.531
And so just reminding yourself of that,

00:04:26.531 --> 00:04:29.123
that you are mortal, you will die,

00:04:29.123 --> 00:04:32.049
and you have things way
better than most people

00:04:32.049 --> 00:04:34.904
can help lift you out of a bad situation,

00:04:34.904 --> 00:04:36.089
a negative situation.

00:04:36.089 --> 00:04:37.278
You're feeling sorry for yourself,

00:04:37.278 --> 00:04:38.111
you're feeling down,

00:04:38.111 --> 00:04:40.315
you're feeling upset that
you didn't get that goal

00:04:40.315 --> 00:04:42.164
or it's not happening fast enough for you,

00:04:42.164 --> 00:04:45.290
or you got rejected or whatever
reason you're upset for.

00:04:45.290 --> 00:04:46.574
I think it's really important

00:04:46.574 --> 00:04:49.168
to pull from opposite
spectrums at the same time,

00:04:49.168 --> 00:04:50.742
I think it's really important to be

00:04:50.742 --> 00:04:53.420
insanely grateful for
everything that you have

00:04:53.420 --> 00:04:54.973
but also want more.

00:04:54.973 --> 00:04:59.088
If you play only on one side
it's going to be hard for you.

00:04:59.088 --> 00:05:01.143
If you only are super grateful

00:05:01.143 --> 00:05:02.626
for everything that you have in your life,

00:05:02.626 --> 00:05:04.532
and life is amazing and wonderful,

00:05:04.532 --> 00:05:07.717
and you're just so grateful
to be in existence,

00:05:07.717 --> 00:05:10.951
then you're never pushing
yourself to get better,

00:05:10.951 --> 00:05:12.955
you're never pushing yourself to do more.

00:05:12.955 --> 00:05:15.419
And, in my opinion, if
you have the ability

00:05:15.419 --> 00:05:17.170
to help others and to do more

00:05:17.170 --> 00:05:19.709
then you have the
responsibility to do it as well.

00:05:19.709 --> 00:05:22.481
And so if you have a lot of
insane talents and skills

00:05:22.481 --> 00:05:24.651
and you're not putting
them to use to help others

00:05:24.651 --> 00:05:26.097
because you're just so grateful

00:05:26.097 --> 00:05:27.461
that life is so wonderful right now,

00:05:27.461 --> 00:05:29.221
it's not pushing you to do more,

00:05:29.221 --> 00:05:30.977
then that's not great.

00:05:30.977 --> 00:05:33.136
On the flip side, if you have no gratitude

00:05:33.136 --> 00:05:34.242
and you're just always wanting more,

00:05:34.242 --> 00:05:35.688
and always pushing, always driving

00:05:35.688 --> 00:05:38.381
and always seeking to do
better, no goal is good enough,

00:05:38.381 --> 00:05:40.997
and just push, push, push, push,

00:05:40.997 --> 00:05:42.930
you're not going to be happy either,

00:05:42.930 --> 00:05:45.542
you're going to probably burn
out and crash at some point.

00:05:45.542 --> 00:05:47.039
You're never going to stop and think

00:05:47.039 --> 00:05:48.948
about everything that
you've done and accomplish

00:05:48.948 --> 00:05:52.643
and be a happy, whole kind of human being,

00:05:52.643 --> 00:05:54.009
and that's going to impact you,

00:05:54.009 --> 00:05:55.086
it's going to impact your family,

00:05:55.086 --> 00:05:57.243
it's going to impact the
people you're trying to reach.

00:05:57.243 --> 00:06:00.497
So I think both, having
insane gratitude --

00:06:00.497 --> 00:06:01.464
If you lost everything,

00:06:01.464 --> 00:06:03.528
if I lost my YouTube channel right now,

00:06:03.528 --> 00:06:05.849
if I couldn't post another
video I'd be really sad,

00:06:05.849 --> 00:06:06.692
but I'd also be really grateful

00:06:06.692 --> 00:06:08.748
for the impact that I have had,

00:06:08.748 --> 00:06:10.541
for all the subscribers that I've touched,

00:06:10.541 --> 00:06:11.744
for the all the lives of the people

00:06:11.744 --> 00:06:13.103
who have watched the videos,

00:06:13.103 --> 00:06:14.425
insanely grateful for that.

00:06:14.425 --> 00:06:16.500
And I want to do more,

00:06:16.500 --> 00:06:18.384
I know I can do more, I
know I can push harder,

00:06:18.384 --> 00:06:21.029
I know I can do better, I
know I need to grind more,

00:06:21.029 --> 00:06:23.810
I know I need to create
better content for you guys.

00:06:23.810 --> 00:06:27.091
So I think having both at the same

00:06:27.091 --> 00:06:30.321
and trying to pull from both,
depending on where you're at.

00:06:30.321 --> 00:06:32.087
You know, if you're comfortable

00:06:32.087 --> 00:06:33.426
then you need more of this side,

00:06:33.426 --> 00:06:35.940
you need more of "I need to
do better, I can do more".

00:06:35.940 --> 00:06:37.764
And if you're being too hard in yourself

00:06:37.764 --> 00:06:39.872
then maybe you need a little
bit of perspective and say,

00:06:39.872 --> 00:06:41.040
"I've really done a lot too,

00:06:41.040 --> 00:06:42.795
"I need to be grateful for what I have".

00:06:42.795 --> 00:06:45.265
That mix, I find, really helps balance me,

00:06:45.265 --> 00:06:47.322
and hopefully provides some ammunition

00:06:47.322 --> 00:06:49.028
and guidance for you as well.

00:06:49.028 --> 00:06:50.990
So the question today is, I'm curious,

00:06:50.990 --> 00:06:55.489
how do you balance gratitude,
conscience of your mortality

00:06:55.489 --> 00:06:58.298
and pushing and striving
and wanting to do more?

00:06:58.298 --> 00:06:59.562
I'd love to hear your thoughts,

00:06:59.562 --> 00:07:01.151
please share down the comments below.

00:07:01.151 --> 00:07:03.248
I also want to give a quick
shout to Daniel Morrow.

00:07:03.248 --> 00:07:05.529
Daniel, thank you so much for
picking up a copy of my book,

00:07:05.529 --> 00:07:06.775
"Your One Word".

00:07:06.775 --> 00:07:08.108
It really, really means a lot to me, man,

00:07:08.108 --> 00:07:10.090
and I hope you're enjoying the read.

00:07:10.090 --> 00:07:11.672
So thank you, guys, again for watching.

00:07:11.672 --> 00:07:12.631
I believe in you.

00:07:12.631 --> 00:07:14.677
I hope you continue to
believe in yourself.

00:07:14.677 --> 00:07:16.975
And remember your one word is,

00:07:16.975 --> 00:07:18.211
and I'll see you again tomorrow morning

00:07:18.211 --> 00:07:20.833
for another shot of Entspresso.

00:07:20.833 --> 00:07:23.288
♫ I wake up every morning

00:07:23.288 --> 00:07:26.705
♫ Espresso keep me going

00:07:29.902 --> 00:07:32.624
- First of all, with the man in the cave

00:07:32.624 --> 00:07:36.291
and this idea and this
thought of the enemy.

00:07:38.428 --> 00:07:42.580
And that was a thought
that used to drive me,

00:07:42.580 --> 00:07:46.887
and kind of haunt me
and make me get up early

00:07:46.887 --> 00:07:49.471
and work hard to push myself,

00:07:49.471 --> 00:07:52.721
because I knew that somewhere out there

00:07:57.084 --> 00:08:01.251
there was an enemy, a real
enemy, a real man, a person,

00:08:02.394 --> 00:08:05.061
a human that was waiting for me,

00:08:07.056 --> 00:08:09.269
and that was preparing for me.

00:08:09.269 --> 00:08:11.269
And, therefore, I needed

00:08:15.031 --> 00:08:18.080
to prepare for him, I needed to be ready,

00:08:18.080 --> 00:08:20.802
I needed to be the things
I always talk about,

00:08:20.802 --> 00:08:24.969
I needed to be stronger and
faster and smarter and better,

00:08:26.911 --> 00:08:30.494
so that when we did
meet on the battlefield

00:08:33.671 --> 00:08:36.754
I would be ready for that rendezvous,

00:08:37.622 --> 00:08:39.955
for that meeting, that fate,

00:08:42.013 --> 00:08:43.013
that battle.

00:08:45.323 --> 00:08:48.307
And that thought, that
thought of the enemy,

00:08:48.307 --> 00:08:50.724
yes, it absolutely fueled me.

00:08:54.756 --> 00:08:58.923
And when I was a leader in the
SEAL teams in charge of men

00:09:00.790 --> 00:09:02.957
it was even more profound,

00:09:03.896 --> 00:09:07.563
because I was thinking
about thar rendezvous

00:09:08.704 --> 00:09:11.395
for everybody that I led,
everyone I was in charged of,

00:09:11.395 --> 00:09:13.395
everyone that I trained.

00:09:15.636 --> 00:09:19.803
And I felt that burden, the
burden of responsibility

00:09:22.044 --> 00:09:25.627
to prepare those men
and protect those men,

00:09:28.067 --> 00:09:30.567
those frogman, those warriors.

00:09:33.812 --> 00:09:34.812
My brothers.

00:09:40.331 --> 00:09:41.998
And it was my burden

00:09:44.697 --> 00:09:47.780
to train those guys and prepare them.

00:09:52.111 --> 00:09:53.444
And that burden,

00:09:54.641 --> 00:09:56.394
it may have made me a little bit crazy,

00:09:56.394 --> 00:10:00.477
a little bit paranoid, a
little bit over the top,

00:10:04.689 --> 00:10:07.106
but I didn't really know any,

00:10:10.965 --> 00:10:12.132
any other way.

00:10:13.151 --> 00:10:15.734
(solemn music)

00:10:19.926 --> 00:10:20.926
And, so now,

00:10:25.616 --> 00:10:26.783
I am no longer

00:10:30.400 --> 00:10:31.400
a combatant.

00:10:34.527 --> 00:10:37.194
I no longer prepare men for war.

00:10:41.111 --> 00:10:42.194
So the drive,

00:10:44.609 --> 00:10:48.442
and the motivation, is
from a different place.

00:10:54.836 --> 00:10:56.919
It's from a solemn place.

00:11:00.598 --> 00:11:03.765
The drive now or the motivation now is

00:11:05.284 --> 00:11:08.117
not really from the enemy anymore.

00:11:12.802 --> 00:11:15.969
Now it's from my friends, my brothers.

00:11:19.731 --> 00:11:20.564
It's from

00:11:22.439 --> 00:11:24.356
those SEALs that I knew

00:11:36.582 --> 00:11:37.415
and that I

00:11:43.736 --> 00:11:46.319
cared about more than anything.

00:11:50.213 --> 00:11:52.213
And that they sacrificed

00:11:56.648 --> 00:11:57.481
everything

00:12:01.739 --> 00:12:02.989
for us, for me.

00:12:04.810 --> 00:12:08.227
Those guys, they gave their lives for us.

00:12:09.914 --> 00:12:13.081
(active solemn music)

00:12:20.377 --> 00:12:24.044
And now I cannot help
but think and remember

00:12:28.196 --> 00:12:31.446
that every breath that we take is a ...

00:12:35.385 --> 00:12:37.968
It's a gift, it's a sacred gift

00:12:39.889 --> 00:12:41.139
from those men.

00:12:43.216 --> 00:12:46.272
Every day we have, ever sunrise,

00:12:46.272 --> 00:12:50.439
every thought and every smile
and every laugh is a gift.

00:12:52.102 --> 00:12:55.269
(active solemn music)

00:12:58.572 --> 00:13:01.072
And I will treasure that gift,

00:13:04.148 --> 00:13:05.648
that gift of life,

00:13:09.414 --> 00:13:13.581
and I will not let it go to
waste, not one second of it.

00:13:17.893 --> 00:13:21.318
And I'll cherish every moment of it,

00:13:21.318 --> 00:13:22.901
and I will live it,

00:13:24.943 --> 00:13:26.110
I will live it

00:13:30.369 --> 00:13:31.619
in their memory

00:13:36.463 --> 00:13:38.046
and in their honor.

